    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d273">

                <pb facs="0525" n="505" xml:id="pg505"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BC
                    Armaments/11–2048: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State, in
                        Paris, to the Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-20T18:00:00+01:00">November 20,
                            1948—6 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Delga 858. Re Gadel 542 November 19.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d273-f1"/>
                    USDel and other delegations believe approved
                    disarmament resolution offers opportunity to place work of CCA on new and satisfactory basis. Urge
                    postponement inter-Departmental conferences and Department action until return
                        USDel, particularly Page Smith and Osborn
                    acquainted with latest discussions other delegations Paris.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d273-f1" n="1" xml:id="d273-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram Gadel 542 read as follows: “Dept like
                    have any comment other Dels and estimate USDel
                    on CCA continuing present order plan work or any
                    deviation therefrom resulting from GA approved
                    disarmament resolution and discussions leading to its adoption.” (501.BC Armaments/11–1948)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
